{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "60b2ac1b-21a4-87c0-be12-acafa46561ab",
  "created_at": "2026-01-27T11:28:18-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Finance",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Angela Grasso",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Luis Barros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:16:31-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Finance department, this is Luis. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:16:38-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Luis. Thank you. My name is Angela Grasso. I am calling about my property tax bill. I think there is a mistake on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:16:55-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, we can look at that. What kind of mistake are we talking about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:17:05-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The square footage of the house. The bill says it is, um, one moment, I have it here. Twenty-eight hundred square feet. But it is not that big. It is a two-family, and it is much smaller."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:17:29-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Twenty-eight hundred. Got it. What's the property address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:17:35-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is three fifty-five Kingston Avenue. In the Historic Hill, near the top part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:17:45-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three fifty-five Kingston. And you're the owner?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:17:50-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I am the owner. I am the landlord. I rent the two apartments. I live somewhere else."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:18:02-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Do you know what the square footage should be?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:18:09-05:00",
      "duration": 23,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "When I bought it, the paper said about eighteen hundred. So there is a difference of one thousand. That is a lot, no? Tá bem, I mean, it is a big difference for the tax."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:18:32-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It could be, yeah. A thousand square feet is not a rounding error. Let me pull up the record. Give me a second."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:18:48-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, of course. Take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:18:53-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, I am in the car, so there is some noise. My daughter is in the back."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:19:05-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, I can hear you fine. Okay, I've got the property card here. It does show twenty-eight hundred gross. Does the house have a finished attic or a basement apartment?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:19:26-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No basement apartment. The attic, it is a storage room only. Not finished. Maybe the person counted it, I do not know."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:19:41-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's possible. Sometimes an attic or an old addition gets counted when it shouldn't. So here's how it works. The assessor's office is the one who fixes the record. I can't change the square footage from finance."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:20:05-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. So I should speak to the assessor. Is there a form for that?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:20:16-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You'd request a review of the assessment. They'll probably want your documents, like the purchase papers or a floor plan, and they may want to come measure."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:20:34-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. They can come inside? That is fine. My tenants, I will tell them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:20:44-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mom, one second. She is asking me why the house is big on the paper. She is, um, fifteen, she asks everything. Sorry."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Tell her the city's wondering the same thing. Nothing wrong with questions."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:09-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "She says thank you. She is not saying that, but I say it for her."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:19-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fair enough. So, you said there's a bill in front of you. Is it the current one, the fiscal year bill?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, the one that came in the mail, December I think. The next payment is due soon, no?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:45-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me check what's showing. Hold on a moment."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:52-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. I wait."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:21:55-05:00",
      "duration": 27,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, I'm back. Your third quarter is due in a few days, the end of this month. If the assessment gets corrected, any change would be adjusted afterward, but I'd still treat the bill as due until someone tells you otherwise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:22:22-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I see. So I pay the bill, and then if they fix it, I get the money back, or it goes to the next one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:22:39-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Usually it's a credit or a refund, depending on how it lands. The assessor's office can explain the details on that part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:22:54-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. That is clear. Now, I have another question. I heard there is an exemption. For a landlord, maybe, or for the owner. I do not know the right word for it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:23:15-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There are a few exemptions. Which one are you thinking about? Owner-occupied, veteran, elderly, disability?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:23:25-05:00",
      "duration": 28,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hmm. A friend told me there is one for the house if the owner lives in it. But I do not live there. Maybe I am not eligible. I only want to ask for the form number, so I can read it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:23:53-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. If you don't live there, the owner-occupied type wouldn't apply to you, since it's for a primary residence. But the form number you'd have to get from the assessor's office. I don't want to read you the wrong one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:24:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. So you do not have the number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:24:25-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not in front of me, no, and exemption forms change from year to year. I can transfer you to the assessor and they can tell you the number and whether you'd even qualify."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:24:47-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. That would be good. Can I ask, are they open now? It is eleven, a little after."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:25:00-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They should be in. Weekday, mid-morning. Let me give you the quick version of what to say. Tell them the address, the square footage on the card, and what you think it should be."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:25:22-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Three fifty-five Kingston, twenty-eight hundred, and I think eighteen hundred. And also the exemption form number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:25:33-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. You've got it down better than most people. Anything else on the finance side before I send you over?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:25:47-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Just one thing. Last weekend we had the snow and then the rain. The roof of that house, I am worried it may have a leak, but that is not for you. I will call the tenants."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:11-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's a building matter, not tax. Hope the roof held up. Okay, I'm going to transfer you. If the line drops, call back and ask for assessing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:30-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you very much, Luis. You were very helpful."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:37-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Anytime. Hang on."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Mom, no, wait, it is still ringing. Okay, I wait."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:47-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, Ms. Grasso, it's ringing through but they're not picking up. Looks like it went to voicemail."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:26:59-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh. Then what do I do?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:27:04-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can leave a message with your name, the address, and your callback number. Or I can take the message and walk it over. Which do you prefer?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:27:23-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If you can do that, please. It is easier. My number is four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-eight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:27:33-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-eight. And it's about the wrong square footage at three fifty-five Kingston, and you want the exemption form number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:27:47-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. That is all correct. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:27:52-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'll get it to them today. They usually call back within a day or two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:28:02-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Good. Have a good day, Luis."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:28:07-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Drive safe with the back seat committee."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-27T11:28:14-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, I will. Obrigada. Goodbye."
    }
  ],
